# workspace-forbidden: directories no agent may start in (see
# compartments.md). vm-setup.sh installs this in
# /usr/local/libexec/bulkhead/; bulkhead-workspace reads it.
#
# One shell "case" pattern per line, matched against the real path of
# both the current directory and its workspace. A leading "~/" means
# your home directory. bulkhead-workspace also refuses ~ and
# everything above it, in code, since that can't be one pattern.

# These hold every workspace (and so every dossier).
~/projects
~/sensitive
# Your configuration, keys, and state (e.g., ~/.ssh, ~/.config), and
# the central dossiers (~/.local/state/bulkhead/dossiers).
~/.*
# A workspace's dossier is data about it that its agent mustn't control.
*.dossier
*.dossier/*
# Shared with other users, who could plant files there first (e.g., a
# workspace's .tmp).
/tmp
/tmp/*
/var/tmp
/var/tmp/*
/dev/shm
/dev/shm/*
